1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:52,719
‪It's my fault.

3
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:56,514
‪Because of me…

4
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,597
‪EPISODE 5

5
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:41,684
‪Mr. Ma?

6
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:46,898
‪Gang-uk.

7
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,318
‪Oh, no…

8
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,447
‪Because of me,

9
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:58,701
‪you turned into a ghost already
‪and came to see me?

10
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:02,664
‪Oh, no…

11
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,460
‪Oh, gosh…

12
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,220
‪I'm not a ghost.

13
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,390
‪I'm alive.

14
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:15,904
‪But before, I definitely saw you…

15
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,661
‪Gang-uk!

16
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:27,290
‪-Charge to 200 joules.
‪-Charging to 200.

17
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:29,834
‪-Clear.
‪-Mr. Ma!

18
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:32,211
‪-Mr. Ma!
‪-Clear.

19
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:33,713
‪Mr. Ma.

20
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:34,672
‪Clear.

21
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,222
‪It worked. We have a pulse.

22
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:45,433
‪He's back. He's okay.

23
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:54,567
‪You're alive?

24
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:08,248
‪Are you sure you're really alive?

25
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:09,791
‪I am.

26
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:13,253
‪My head hurts a bit,

27
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:17,173
‪but I'm quite all right
‪for someone who got hit by a car.

28
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:26,057
‪I thought you'd actually died
‪because of me.

29
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:28,810
‪Do you know how scared I was?

30
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:31,854
‪I'm sorry.

31
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:33,690
‪You're not hurt anywhere, right?

32
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:38,903
‪Mr. Ma!

33
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:43,324
‪You need to come.

34
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:50,373
‪-Is there something wrong?
‪-No.

35
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:54,127
‪There's nothing
‪terribly wrong with him right now,

36
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:57,380
‪but the doctor wants to run
‪a few tests, just in case.

37
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:59,882
‪That gave us all quite a scare.

38
00:05:00,591 --> 00:05:02,010
‪You still seem to be in shock.

39
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:07,598
‪We should get going then.

40
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:09,142
‪Take good care of Mr. Ma for us.

41
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:10,226
‪You go on ahead.

42
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,478
‪-I don't mind staying behind.
‪-What?

43
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,980
‪It's been a long day. Go on home.

44
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:17,442
‪It's late, and your wife will be worried.

45
00:05:17,525 --> 00:05:19,360
‪Why would she worry
‪with everything that's happening?

46
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:20,862
‪One of us should stay behind.

47
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:22,113
‪Yes, that one person…

48
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:25,742
‪What? Oh, she's…

49
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,618
‪-She's going to stay?
‪-Yes.

50
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,329
‪-Yes, she's staying.
‪-She is?

51
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:31,748
‪Take good care of him for us. Thank you.

52
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:34,167
‪-At least until he falls asleep…
‪-Take care.

53
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:35,585
‪Hey.

54
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:42,258
‪Drink lots of water to flush
‪the contrast medium out of your system.

55
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:43,843
‪You'll be hospitalized for the night,

56
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:47,430
‪and the doctor will give you the results
‪in the morning.

57
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:48,681
‪Okay. Thank you.

58
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:49,849
‪You're welcome.

59
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:55,855
‪CT IMAGING ROOM

60
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:17,960
‪You're still here, Yeo-ri?

61
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:20,254
‪The one month isn't up yet.

62
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:24,175
‪It's not over until the moon
‪disappears at dawn.

63
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:27,970
‪Try to keep up.

64
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:29,514
‪Okay.

65
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:10,596
‪They agreed not to come into your room.

66
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,015
‪How did you make them agree to that?

67
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:14,976
‪I told them the usual,

68
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:17,520
‪that they can come to my place
‪if they really want to talk.

69
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:22,233
‪Did this happen
‪because we celebrated a day early?

70
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:26,946
‪What's meant to happen happens,
‪regardless of such things.

71
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:30,199
‪Only seeing and hearing
‪what everyone else does…

72
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:33,619
‪I can't believe
‪that's something worth celebrating.

73
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:37,457
‪Yeo-ri.

74
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:40,543
‪The moon will set soon.
‪You must be exhausted, so go home.

75
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:45,173
‪I'd rather stay where I can be at ease
‪than go home and be anxious.

76
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:50,136
‪Your month is almost up for good,
‪so I'll rest here with you.

77
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:01,314
‪I didn't get to ask you
‪because things got a bit hectic.

78
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:03,024
‪Why did Park Seung-jae abduct you?

79
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:04,609
‪I'm the one who put him behind bars.

80
00:08:06,402 --> 00:08:09,280
‪I think he caught on to my secret.

81
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,657
‪But how?

82
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:14,494
‪That's a family matter.

83
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:21,042
‪How did you know where to find me anyway?

84
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:23,503
‪Well…

85
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:29,884
‪FIND ME

86
00:08:29,967 --> 00:08:32,845
‪FIND ME

87
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:36,307
‪I think a ghost told me.

88
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,018
‪-A ghost?
‪-Yes.

89
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:41,562
‪Come in.

90
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:43,940
‪Hello.

91
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,484
‪-I'm here to change your IV bag.
‪-Okay.

92
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,862
‪Can you be gentle this time?
‪It hurt earlier.

93
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,864
‪-I'm scared of needles.
‪-Okay.

94
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:56,869
‪HANKUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

95
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:33,781
<i>‪Because of me,</i>

96
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,784
‪you turned into a ghost already
‪and came to see me?

97
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,331
‪Oh, no…

98
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:49,190
‪I think the one month is up now.

99
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,319
‪I should go do some stretching.

100
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:13,464
‪REGIONAL EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

101
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:16,092
‪I told you I'd be fine.
‪You didn't have to worry.

102
00:11:17,259 --> 00:11:20,554
‪Still, I feel much better
‪after seeing the results myself.

103
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:27,728
‪I guess today is day one
‪of not seeing ghosts.

104
00:11:28,437 --> 00:11:30,147
‪Yes, based on my experiences so far.

105
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,357
‪I really won't see them

106
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,317
‪anymore, right?

107
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:40,449
‪I find it really hard to believe,

108
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:44,662
‪but knowing such supernatural beings
‪exist in our world today…

109
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:46,956
‪I know, right?

110
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:50,918
‪Anyway, congratulations.

111
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,629
‪You can go back to your normal life now.

112
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:56,924
‪I feel bad that I'm the only one
‪who gets off like this.

113
00:11:57,007 --> 00:11:57,842
‪Don't be.

114
00:11:58,426 --> 00:12:02,471
‪It's a relief that you, at least,
‪can escape this fate.

115
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:05,808
‪Yeo-ri.

116
00:12:08,602 --> 00:12:10,938
‪Even if you were to
‪continue seeing ghosts,

117
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:13,023
‪that wouldn't mean I'd stop seeing them.

118
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:17,695
‪We can't shake hands anymore,

119
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:20,156
‪so let's part ways here.

120
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:25,286
‪From now on,
‪let's never cross paths again.

121
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:41,760
‪Take care.

122
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:44,805
‪Thanks for everything.

123
00:14:03,175 --> 00:14:05,344
‪REHEAT THE RICE AND SOUP AND EAT WELL

124
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:17,940
<i>‪From now on,</i>
<i>‪let's never cross paths again.</i>

125
00:14:19,149 --> 00:14:20,234
<i>‪Take care.</i>

126
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:22,987
<i>‪Thanks for everything.</i>

127
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,705
‪Just to be clear,
‪I never told you to kidnap her.

128
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:36,041
‪And don't call me like this again,
‪not even through your lawyer.

129
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,418
<i>‪Wait, Ha-ri, I--</i>

130
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:39,503
‪Hello? Cheon Ha-ri!

131
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:41,005
‪Damn it.

132
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:52,892
‪The assemblyman said
‪he can't help you anymore.

133
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:55,853
‪He told me to inform you
‪that there'd be no more favors.

134
00:14:58,856 --> 00:14:59,773
‪Wait…

135
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:02,318
‪Damn it.

136
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:09,158
‪Mr. Ma. Are you all right?

137
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:11,410
‪I'm still a bit sore. Did you have lunch?

138
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:13,954
‪I told you I put in a day off for you.

139
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:16,040
‪Why are you so stubborn?

140
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:18,792
‪Come on, there's a warrant hearing later.

141
00:15:18,876 --> 00:15:22,713
‪I told you the chief prosecutor
‪can handle that for you.

142
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:25,424
‪-Mr. Ma.
‪-Yeah?

143
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:27,676
‪You need to see this.

144
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:28,636
‪Why?

145
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:30,679
‪What is it?

146
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:32,181
‪PARK SEUNG-JAE ABDUCTED CEO CHEON YEO-RI,
‪MOTIVE UNDER INVESTIGATION

147
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,558
‪Reporters are already
‪swarming outside Reina.

148
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:35,935
‪PARK SEUNG-JAE ABDUCTED CEO CHEON YEO-RI

149
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:37,603
<i>‪Please leave.</i>
<i>‪We'll explain some other time.</i>

150
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:44,610
‪Mr. Ma.

151
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:46,528
‪-She won't do any interviews.
‪-Just let us…

152
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:49,073
‪-No, you can't…
‪-Will you stop it?

153
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:51,909
‪-Just a few shots.
‪-No way!

154
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:54,620
‪-Stop! Get back!
‪-Don't take any photos!

155
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,622
‪-You can't.
‪-No photos or filming!

156
00:15:56,705 --> 00:15:58,874
‪-Can we get a comment?
‪-No photos, please!

157
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,626
‪-What happened?
‪-Don't take photos!

158
00:16:00,709 --> 00:16:03,170
‪-Is everything we heard true?
‪-I said, no photos.

159
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:05,506
‪-Any further comments?
‪-Just a brief statement, please.

160
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:07,549
‪Gosh, there are so many of them.

161
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:09,134
‪-How are you now?
‪-We won't take long.

162
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:11,261
‪-Any comments, please?
‪-Please stop.

163
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:21,271
‪-Can you tell us anything?
‪-Please step back.

164
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:24,066
‪-Please step back.
‪-Excuse me, Ms. Cheon.

165
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:25,776
‪-Move back.
‪-Can you do an interview?

166
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:44,503
‪Are you dating Ms. Cheon?

167
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,588
‪Should there be
‪any unverified information,

168
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,592
‪speculative articles,
‪or photos distributed…

169
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:55,431
‪Reina will take strong legal action.

170
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:58,308
‪Direct your questions
‪to the secretaries' office,

171
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:01,729
‪and please step back.

172
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,591
‪I should've gotten here sooner.

173
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:40,976
‪Are you all right?

174
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:42,352
‪Yeah.

175
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:44,605
‪Thanks.

176
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:59,161
‪I'm sorry for causing you concern.

177
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:01,538
‪Were you hurt anywhere?

178
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:04,374
‪Should I call Dr. Kim?

179
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:07,461
‪Let's get you admitted for some tests.

180
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:08,420
‪No.

181
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:11,548
‪There's an inspection for the GA21 banquet
‪by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs today.

182
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:14,134
‪I came to work thinking only of that.

183
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:16,887
‪We'll take strong action

184
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:21,433
‪against not only Park Seung-jae,
‪but his father Assemblyman Park too.

185
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:24,561
‪Don't worry about them
‪and look after yourself.

186
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,105
‪Okay.

187
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:29,942
‪I do have more questions to ask you,

188
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:31,443
‪but let's leave it at that for today.

189
00:18:32,027 --> 00:18:34,404
‪Just handle the inspection,
‪then go home and rest.

190
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:37,449
‪Don't worry about me, Grandma.

191
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:46,750
‪What is it?

192
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:48,961
‪What do you want?

193
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:49,920
‪What?

194
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:52,214
‪The secretaries confirmed it.

195
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:57,219
‪You visited Park Seung-jae in prison twice
‪before he kidnapped me.

196
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:59,763
‪Is that when you put him up to kidnap me?

197
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,306
‪What do you mean, kidnap you?

198
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,349
‪Even if I…

199
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,603
‪Yes, I did visit him.

200
00:19:07,104 --> 00:19:09,064
‪But only because he begged me to.

201
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,150
‪I only went and saw him.

202
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:14,444
‪Park Seung-jae isn't
‪the tight-lipped type,

203
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,114
‪so I'm sure the investigation
‪will reveal everything.

204
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:19,658
‪Cheon Ha-ri.

205
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:25,622
‪You can tell a lot about a person
‪by what they do.

206
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:31,628
‪Take a long, hard look
‪at everything you've done so far,

207
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:32,754
‪because that's your future.

208
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:36,216
‪What do you mean?
‪You're not making any sense.

209
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,093
‪If you don't understand,
‪just memorize it.

210
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:40,012
‪"Don't do bad things."

211
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:41,889
‪Also,

212
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:44,433
‪I'm not letting this slide.

213
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:46,518
‪Don't think I did.

214
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:01,617
‪Was Ha-ri behind it?

215
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:05,662
‪She did visit him in prison,
‪but that doesn't prove anything.

216
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,666
‪By the way, what are you doing in Seoul?

217
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,543
‪That took you long enough.

218
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:13,921
‪I called you as soon as I arrived.

219
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:17,633
‪G1A Group is trying to sell Fiel Seoul.

220
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:20,302
‪-Is CL going to acquire it?
‪-Yeah.

221
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:23,889
‪It's the only big resort brand
‪in the northern Seoul area.

222
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:27,601
‪I heard their debt ratio
‪is on the higher side.

223
00:20:27,684 --> 00:20:29,061
‪That's true,

224
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:32,314
‪but we have a financial arm
‪that can handle the aftermath.

225
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:36,235
‪Anyway, do you know how shocked I was
‪during my breakfast meeting?

226
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:40,072
‪First, it was in Jeju Island,
‪and now this.

227
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:41,865
‪Things keep going wrong.

228
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:43,450
‪What happened in Jeju was on us.

229
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:48,747
‪I think I'll be in Seoul
‪until the acquisition is finalized.

230
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:50,123
‪You'll call me, right?

231
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:51,625
‪What?

232
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:53,460
‪I knew it.

233
00:20:53,543 --> 00:20:55,045
‪You owe me a meal.

234
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:56,964
‪Right.

235
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:58,423
‪Yes, of course.

236
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:00,842
‪Well, when are you free?

237
00:21:03,178 --> 00:21:07,057
‪Instead of going somewhere to eat,
‪you can accompany me elsewhere.

238
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,976
‪Yeeon Museum of Art.

239
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:12,354
‪They're unveiling an artifact
‪they excavated recently.

240
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:14,606
‪I have a meeting there
‪that my mother arranged.

241
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:16,441
‪Yeeon?

242
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:19,278
‪The director there is pretty influential.

243
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:22,698
‪This new artifact should interest you too,

244
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:24,741
‪since it's not entirely unrelated
‪to your major.

245
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:26,743
‪What is it?

246
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:28,870
‪I'll send you a link
‪to the director's interview.

247
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,336
<i>‪From what my mom told me,</i>

248
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:39,589
<i>‪she seems to be seeing</i>
<i>‪some prosecutor pretty often.</i>

249
00:21:46,221 --> 00:21:47,055
‪Yes, Secretary Oh.

250
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,599
‪I need you to look into someone for me.

251
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:52,394
‪Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk from the Seoul
‪Central District Prosecutors' Office.

252
00:21:52,477 --> 00:21:53,395
‪Min-hwan.

253
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:03,488
‪THE HOLY BIBLE

254
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:13,040
‪-So you've finally settled on one?
‪-No.

255
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:15,000
‪I went back to having no religion.

256
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:16,710
‪What?

257
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:18,295
‪I switched back.

258
00:22:19,046 --> 00:22:19,880
‪I see.

259
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:38,607
‪I don't believe it.

260
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,197
‪Jeez.

261
00:22:50,827 --> 00:22:51,953
‪Why did you want to see me?

262
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:55,457
‪How much do you know about Yeo-ri?

263
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:00,128
‪More than you think.

264
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:01,797
‪I doubt that.

265
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,466
‪You know she broke off her engagement

266
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:06,468
‪with the son of Cha & Yul's
‪managing partner, right?

267
00:23:06,551 --> 00:23:08,678
‪I only heard about it
‪since I was abroad at the time.

268
00:23:08,762 --> 00:23:11,598
‪Then do you know why they broke it off?

269
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:14,726
‪Do I have to know why?

270
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:17,646
‪You told me before

271
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:20,816
‪that if you care about someone,
‪you learn all about them.

272
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:23,735
‪I thought you'd naturally want to know
‪why they broke it off.

273
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:27,781
‪Don't you want to know?

274
00:23:27,864 --> 00:23:29,741
‪Some rumors started
‪after the engagement fell through.

275
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:30,867
‪Ha-ri.

276
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:34,830
‪If I want to know something,
‪I can look into it myself.

277
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:43,713
‪Oh, that night at the hospital?

278
00:23:43,797 --> 00:23:44,923
‪I remember.

279
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:52,639
‪You're where?

280
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:07,195
‪An anonymous tip-off
‪leading to the discovery of a body.

281
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:10,490
‪Doesn't it feel like <i>‪déjà vu?</i>

282
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:11,867
‪Yes.

283
00:24:27,090 --> 00:24:29,301
‪I don't need extra layers like these.

284
00:25:20,227 --> 00:25:22,020
<i>‪You should go inside and warm up.</i>

285
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:24,606
‪Nice, we did it. High-five?

286
00:25:25,232 --> 00:25:26,566
<i>‪Lend me a hand?</i>

287
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:36,469
‪-Enjoy your lunch.
‪-You too, sir.

288
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:46,187
‪-Enjoy your lunch, sir!
‪-Thank you.

289
00:26:54,237 --> 00:26:56,114
‪Reina Hotel's slush fund allegations?

290
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:57,949
‪Yeah. I sense some rising smoke.

291
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:00,744
‪Rich people use art
‪to launder money, you know.

292
00:27:00,827 --> 00:27:02,912
‪-It's pretty large-scale too.
‪-Come on.

293
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:05,749
‪It smoked a bit,
‪but the fire went out long ago.

294
00:27:15,258 --> 00:27:18,136
‪Ma'am, have you
‪not been sleeping well lately?

295
00:27:19,387 --> 00:27:20,764
‪Why do you ask?

296
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:22,724
‪You look very tired.

297
00:27:32,275 --> 00:27:33,276
‪Who is that?

298
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:36,529
‪That's Director Lee Hwa-yong
‪of the Yeeon Foundation.

299
00:27:37,822 --> 00:27:38,782
<i>‪Yeeon Museum of Art.</i>

300
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:41,659
‪The director there is pretty influential.

301
00:27:43,536 --> 00:27:45,497
‪-Mr. Bong.
‪-Yes?

302
00:27:47,791 --> 00:27:49,751
‪Could you come a little closer?

303
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:51,461
‪Pardon? Oh, sure.

304
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:57,133
‪The artworks displayed at the hotel

305
00:27:57,217 --> 00:28:01,054
‪are brought in by the Art Team
‪through Director Ok,

306
00:28:01,137 --> 00:28:03,264
‪so Gallery Cheon supplies them, right?

307
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:05,016
‪Yes, that is correct.

308
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:08,269
‪Have we ever made
‪a direct purchase from Yeeon?

309
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:11,022
‪No, not as far as I'm aware.

310
00:28:13,858 --> 00:28:16,277
‪Would you like me to look into it?

311
00:28:17,695 --> 00:28:20,865
‪No, I'll bring it up some other time.

312
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:23,410
‪Don't stand too close.

313
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:24,994
‪Oh, right.

314
00:28:28,289 --> 00:28:31,668
<i>‪A 300-year-old love letter</i>
<i>‪written by Joseon-era</i>

315
00:28:31,751 --> 00:28:35,630
<i>‪courtesan-turned-poet Hwagyeongdang,</i>
<i>‪whose story was likened</i>

316
00:28:35,713 --> 00:28:38,341
<i>‪to the 1990 film </i>‪Ghost
<i>‪recently came to light.</i>

317
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:40,677
<i>‪It recently became the talk of the town.</i>

318
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:43,054
<i>‪We asked Lee Hwa-yong,</i>
<i>‪the director of Yeeon Foundation,</i>

319
00:28:43,138 --> 00:28:46,766
<i>‪why she decided</i>
<i>‪to reveal the letter to the public.</i>

320
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:47,767
<i>‪Well…</i>

321
00:28:48,643 --> 00:28:52,480
<i>‪We discovered this love letter</i>
<i>‪while relocating the tomb</i>

322
00:28:52,564 --> 00:28:54,941
<i>‪of my ancestor, Prince Gangpyeong.</i>

323
00:28:55,024 --> 00:28:57,152
<i>‪As many are already aware,</i>

324
00:28:57,235 --> 00:29:00,447
<i>‪the letter shows</i>
<i>‪Hwagyeongdang's </i><i>‪love </i><i>‪for Prince Gangpyeong</i>

325
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:03,199
<i>‪that transcended class and social status.</i>

326
00:29:04,033 --> 00:29:07,620
<i>‪These days, there's so much violence</i>
<i>‪carried out in the name of love,</i>

327
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:10,749
<i>‪so I wanted to remind us</i>
<i>‪what's most important</i>

328
00:29:10,832 --> 00:29:13,501
<i>‪and provide consolation</i>
<i>‪in what little way I can</i>

329
00:29:13,585 --> 00:29:15,003
<i>‪by displaying the letter.</i>

330
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:17,881
<i>‪After the exhibition,</i>

331
00:29:17,964 --> 00:29:21,509
<i>‪I'll respect the wishes of my late father,</i>
<i>‪the foundation's first director,</i>

332
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:23,011
<i>‪and donate it to his alma mater--</i>

333
00:29:31,019 --> 00:29:32,228
‪Great shot.

334
00:29:33,646 --> 00:29:34,647
‪I'm playing decently today.

335
00:29:36,065 --> 00:29:36,983
‪It's really nice.

336
00:29:37,066 --> 00:29:39,903
‪A design that focuses
‪on harmonizing with nature.

337
00:29:39,986 --> 00:29:41,529
‪The layout is daring too.

338
00:29:41,613 --> 00:29:43,364
‪Is it Jackson Nicola's work?

339
00:29:43,448 --> 00:29:45,492
‪I paid a small fortune
‪to get the design right.

340
00:29:46,284 --> 00:29:47,243
‪Come and play often.

341
00:29:47,827 --> 00:29:49,746
‪Just gather a solid group first.

342
00:29:50,580 --> 00:29:51,456
‪Right.

343
00:29:51,956 --> 00:29:55,043
‪You went to school with Cha Gi-u
‪from Cha & Yul Law Firm, right?

344
00:29:55,126 --> 00:29:57,670
‪Yeah, he's one of our members.
‪Should I set up a round with him?

345
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:00,924
‪Sure.

346
00:30:01,007 --> 00:30:01,925
‪Okay.

347
00:30:05,053 --> 00:30:06,346
‪-I need to take this.
‪-Sure.

348
00:30:07,889 --> 00:30:09,015
‪Hey, Yeo-ri.

349
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:14,187
‪Sure, let's go together.

350
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:16,606
‪I'll pick you up.

351
00:30:16,689 --> 00:30:18,233
‪-What is it?
‪-Just get in there.

352
00:30:18,316 --> 00:30:19,692
‪-Hurry up.
‪-What's this about?

353
00:30:20,568 --> 00:30:22,403
‪Come on and sit over there.

354
00:30:23,238 --> 00:30:24,948
‪And drink this. It's the latte you like.

355
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:27,116
‪Sit.

356
00:30:28,034 --> 00:30:28,952
‪What's up?

357
00:30:29,911 --> 00:30:30,912
‪Hey.

358
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:35,083
‪Tell me all you know
‪about what you said in the cafeteria.

359
00:30:35,708 --> 00:30:36,668
‪About what?

360
00:30:37,585 --> 00:30:38,837
‪The Reina Hotel slush fund.

361
00:30:39,420 --> 00:30:41,464
‪Oh, that?

362
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:43,591
‪You want me to talk for free?

363
00:30:43,675 --> 00:30:45,426
‪I got you coffee.

364
00:30:47,846 --> 00:30:49,472
‪How about a meal?

365
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:51,266
‪A meal? I'll buy you food too.

366
00:30:51,349 --> 00:30:52,684
‪Here. Drink this.

367
00:30:52,767 --> 00:30:54,602
‪Not the cafeteria. Somewhere else.

368
00:30:54,686 --> 00:30:56,479
‪Okay, fine.

369
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:58,439
‪What's the smoke you saw?

370
00:30:58,523 --> 00:31:00,608
‪I'll pick the time and location then.

371
00:31:02,193 --> 00:31:04,153
‪Deal. Now start talking.

372
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:05,321
‪This is perfect.

373
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:06,906
‪-We'll make it if we go now.
‪-Where?

374
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:09,617
‪You said I could decide
‪on the time and location.

375
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:11,536
‪Not right now. I have to work late.

376
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:12,787
‪Do that after eating with me.

377
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:14,205
‪-Come along.
‪-But…

378
00:31:14,289 --> 00:31:16,708
‪-Hey, you really need to fix that.
‪-Hurry.

379
00:31:17,208 --> 00:31:18,167
‪Let me get my coat.

380
00:31:19,252 --> 00:31:20,712
‪This is where you wanted to eat?

381
00:31:20,795 --> 00:31:23,172
‪Yeah. I wanted to come
‪to a place like this with you.

382
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:24,507
‪Hey, Gang-uk.

383
00:31:24,591 --> 00:31:27,176
‪What the heck was that about?

384
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:29,679
‪This isn't my taste.
‪Let's go someplace else.

385
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:33,850
‪Then I'll forget all I know
‪about Reina Hotel and its slush fund.

386
00:31:34,809 --> 00:31:36,060
‪What event are we here for?

387
00:31:37,061 --> 00:31:37,937
‪That one.

388
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:41,316
‪You haven't heard of it?
‪It's been a hot topic lately.

389
00:31:41,399 --> 00:31:44,819
‪They're hosting a special unveiling today
‪before showing it to the public.

390
00:31:45,737 --> 00:31:47,447
‪How did you get invited
‪to something like this?

391
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:52,118
‪I got to know the director here
‪while investigating an art theft case.

392
00:31:53,077 --> 00:31:55,288
‪You know, she set me up

393
00:31:55,371 --> 00:31:58,499
‪on a few blind dates with some great guys.

394
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:01,377
‪You could've brought
‪one of them here instead.

395
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:04,631
‪-Why drag poor busy me here?
‪-You're not getting it, are you?

396
00:32:05,131 --> 00:32:06,883
‪I wanted to bring you.

397
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:10,470
‪Fine, whatever.
‪Where are they showing that letter?

398
00:32:10,553 --> 00:32:12,639
‪Probably somewhere indoors. Let's go.

399
00:32:14,182 --> 00:32:15,183
‪It's so pretty.

400
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:39,332
‪WAITING FOR A LOVE LETTER AFTER 300 YEARS

401
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:42,377
‪Hey, I look horrible. Delete it.

402
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:44,128
‪No one told you to scowl.

403
00:32:45,546 --> 00:32:47,256
‪-Hey.
‪-Wow.

404
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:49,759
‪So the 300-year-old love letter
‪is in that glass case?

405
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:51,135
‪It looks like it.

406
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:52,929
‪Prosecutor Im.

407
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:54,389
‪-Hello, Director.
‪-Hi.

408
00:32:54,472 --> 00:32:55,932
‪Thank you for the invitation.

409
00:32:56,015 --> 00:32:58,768
‪-Thanks so much for coming.
‪-Of course.

410
00:32:58,851 --> 00:33:00,186
‪Who might this be?

411
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:03,106
‪He's a colleague of mine,
‪Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk.

412
00:33:03,189 --> 00:33:05,650
‪-I see. Nice to meet you.
‪-It's a pleasure.

413
00:33:05,733 --> 00:33:07,735
‪-Would you come and say hello?
‪-Sure.

414
00:33:40,226 --> 00:33:41,894
‪-Let's go, Ma.
‪-What?

415
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:44,355
‪Let's go.

416
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:45,273
‪Yeo-ri.

417
00:33:46,399 --> 00:33:47,233
‪Right.

418
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:48,901
‪-Let's go.
‪-Let go of me.

419
00:33:58,536 --> 00:33:59,746
‪Yeo-ri.

420
00:34:01,914 --> 00:34:05,585
‪Thank you for making
‪the long journey over.

421
00:34:05,668 --> 00:34:09,338
‪I'm Lee Hwa-yong,
‪Director of the Yeeon Foundation.

422
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:15,219
‪-What are you looking at?
‪-Look straight ahead.

423
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:18,765
‪My late father built
‪the Yeeon Museum of Art

424
00:34:18,848 --> 00:34:21,517
‪where Prince Gangpyeong's
‪residence once stood…

425
00:34:21,601 --> 00:34:24,103
‪Why does he always stare at me like that?

426
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:27,440
‪It makes me emotional
‪that I can unveil the letter here today.

427
00:34:27,523 --> 00:34:31,778
‪I will now unveil the love letter
‪of Hwagyeongdang,

428
00:34:31,861 --> 00:34:35,740
‪who was a great poet of her time
‪and also a respected painter.

429
00:34:58,763 --> 00:34:59,764
‪Is it breaking?

430
00:35:07,355 --> 00:35:09,482
‪-It's about to crack.
‪-Oh, no!

431
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:14,904
‪Ms. Kim.

432
00:35:29,377 --> 00:35:30,586
‪Our apologies.

433
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:33,214
‪This event is cancelled,
‪and we'll inform you of further plans.

434
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:34,423
‪We're very sorry.

435
00:35:35,216 --> 00:35:36,342
‪Please stay calm.

436
00:35:36,425 --> 00:35:38,928
‪You can take the stairs and exit safely.

437
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:41,806
‪We apologize for the disturbance.
‪Show them the way.

438
00:35:42,348 --> 00:35:43,641
‪What on earth was that?

439
00:35:43,724 --> 00:35:45,977
‪-Are you hurt?
‪-Moving a tomb can bring bad luck.

440
00:35:46,060 --> 00:35:47,603
‪-Watch your step.
‪-Is that what happened?

441
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:49,188
‪It must be that.

442
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:51,524
‪Why would a glass case break
‪when no one touched it?

443
00:35:51,607 --> 00:35:52,608
‪I know, right?

444
00:35:53,609 --> 00:35:55,278
‪This doesn't feel right.

445
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:57,238
‪-It feels ominous.
‪-Let's get out of here.

446
00:35:57,321 --> 00:35:59,073
‪Leave slowly, one at a time.

447
00:36:00,116 --> 00:36:02,618
‪-What do you think happened?
‪-The glass shattered.

448
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:05,580
‪-What a shoddy job.
‪-Make sure you have your belongings.

449
00:36:05,663 --> 00:36:08,457
‪-Why would a perfectly fine glass break?
‪-It felt so strange.

450
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:10,126
‪Aren't you coming?

451
00:36:10,209 --> 00:36:11,377
‪I have to go somewhere.

452
00:36:11,460 --> 00:36:13,212
‪-I'll come with you.
‪-No, no.

453
00:36:14,589 --> 00:36:16,591
‪My stomach hurts.
‪I'm going to the bathroom.

454
00:36:16,674 --> 00:36:19,093
‪-You go ahead. Bye.
‪-What?

455
00:36:26,976 --> 00:36:28,853
‪I came here for a meeting
‪at my mother's request.

456
00:36:28,936 --> 00:36:30,605
‪Can I quickly go and say hello?

457
00:36:31,355 --> 00:36:32,732
‪Yeah, sure. Go ahead.

458
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:35,276
‪-Sorry. Look around in the meantime.
‪-Okay.

459
00:36:58,883 --> 00:37:03,179
‪The legal team will file for damages
‪against the glass manufacturer.

460
00:37:03,262 --> 00:37:04,263
‪Our apologies, ma'am.

461
00:37:05,723 --> 00:37:06,682
‪What for?

462
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:09,060
‪Will you make them pay
‪for the broken glass?

463
00:37:09,143 --> 00:37:11,854
‪Is this how you think
‪an unveiling should go?

464
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:14,482
‪What will you do about the humiliation?

465
00:37:15,358 --> 00:37:16,192
‪What?

466
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:20,738
‪Oh, Mr. Kang.

467
00:37:22,531 --> 00:37:24,450
‪-You must've been shocked earlier.
‪-Not at all.

468
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:27,828
‪We'll arrange another unveiling
‪to make up for it.

469
00:37:28,329 --> 00:37:29,330
‪Okay.

470
00:37:52,853 --> 00:37:53,813
‪Hey, Yeo-ri.

471
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:55,982
‪You're still here?

472
00:37:56,649 --> 00:37:57,817
‪Yes.

473
00:37:59,068 --> 00:38:03,072
‪I didn't get to properly say hi earlier
‪when we've met again after a while.

474
00:38:05,449 --> 00:38:06,534
‪How have you been?

475
00:38:07,576 --> 00:38:09,870
‪I've been doing fine, I guess.

476
00:38:10,913 --> 00:38:12,248
‪So we meet again.

477
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:14,750
‪Are you doing well too?

478
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:16,419
‪Yes, of course. I'm great.

479
00:38:19,005 --> 00:38:21,340
‪You seem to have solved
‪another case by the river.

480
00:38:21,424 --> 00:38:23,592
‪That's what I do as usual.

481
00:38:23,676 --> 00:38:24,635
‪Right.

482
00:38:28,931 --> 00:38:29,765
‪Bye then.

483
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:34,770
‪Wait. Just a moment.

484
00:38:39,317 --> 00:38:40,943
‪I'm not doing well, actually.

485
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:45,656
‪The thing is…

486
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:48,826
‪Are you unwell because of the accident?

487
00:38:48,909 --> 00:38:50,161
‪No, it's not that.

488
00:38:53,372 --> 00:38:54,498
‪I still see them.

489
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:57,668
‪I mean,

490
00:38:57,752 --> 00:39:00,004
‪I still see ghosts and I'm struggling.

491
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:02,590
‪No way. That can't be.

492
00:39:02,673 --> 00:39:05,801
‪I still see ghosts all the time,

493
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:07,803
‪and they give me a fright.

494
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:11,432
‪I wasn't sure
‪if I should contact you about it,

495
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:13,225
‪and we happened to meet here today.

496
00:39:15,978 --> 00:39:17,063
‪Then…

497
00:39:17,688 --> 00:39:21,233
‪do you see the ghost that's here with us?

498
00:39:21,317 --> 00:39:22,234
‪What?

499
00:39:23,819 --> 00:39:24,904
‪Yes, I see it.

500
00:39:24,987 --> 00:39:26,113
‪What does it look like?

501
00:39:29,658 --> 00:39:30,826
‪It's wearing <i>‪hanbok</i>‪,

502
00:39:31,327 --> 00:39:32,495
‪the traditional Korean outfit.

503
00:39:35,581 --> 00:39:36,832
‪-What else?
‪-What else?

504
00:39:36,916 --> 00:39:38,459
‪Go on. What does it look like?

505
00:39:40,878 --> 00:39:43,589
‪It's wearing a jade <i>‪binyeo</i>‪,
‪that fancy hairpin, and is very graceful.

506
00:39:44,256 --> 00:39:45,716
‪-What else?
‪-What else?

507
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:48,969
‪Do you see a small black mole
‪under an eye?

508
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:51,013
‪Yes, I do. There's a mole under one eye.

509
00:39:51,097 --> 00:39:53,766
‪-And is there a knife in her mouth?
‪-Yes. I feel her resentment.

510
00:39:53,849 --> 00:39:56,352
‪She's glaring at me
‪with the knife in her mouth…

511
00:39:58,646 --> 00:40:01,690
‪What prosecutor is this good at lying?

512
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:06,404
‪You could tell?

513
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:09,865
‪How did you know it was wearing <i>‪hanbok</i>‪?

514
00:40:10,658 --> 00:40:11,700
‪Well, this place

515
00:40:11,784 --> 00:40:13,994
‪felt like the set of a period drama,

516
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:17,081
‪and those portraits stood out
‪the moment you asked.

517
00:40:18,290 --> 00:40:20,918
‪And the jade <i>‪binyeo</i>‪.
‪Where did that idea come from?

518
00:40:21,001 --> 00:40:24,338
‪People wearing <i>‪hanbok</i>
‪tend to wear one or two of them.

519
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:28,300
‪How did you catch on right away?

520
00:40:31,053 --> 00:40:32,555
‪Because it's not a woman.

521
00:40:33,639 --> 00:40:34,640
‪It's a man.

522
00:40:35,641 --> 00:40:36,642
‪What?

523
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:41,522
‪Then is there really one…

524
00:40:44,024 --> 00:40:45,276
‪next to me?

525
00:40:47,027 --> 00:40:48,737
‪Yes, he's right next to you.

526
00:40:54,994 --> 00:40:56,829
‪I'm sorry, I'll be careful.

527
00:40:58,497 --> 00:41:01,542
‪Ms. Cheon,
‪is there something wrong with this place?

528
00:41:02,668 --> 00:41:04,837
‪Well, I can't say for sure just yet.

529
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:07,923
‪I need to look into it some more.

530
00:41:08,007 --> 00:41:09,675
‪Right. I see.

531
00:41:13,053 --> 00:41:13,971
‪Ms. Cheon.

532
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:16,432
‪Why don't we work together?

533
00:41:17,349 --> 00:41:18,184
‪On what?

534
00:41:18,267 --> 00:41:21,061
‪I don't know what exactly,

535
00:41:21,145 --> 00:41:23,147
‪but this feels huge and historical.

536
00:41:23,898 --> 00:41:27,359
‪It might be better to cooperate
‪than to work on your own.

537
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:30,696
‪You can handle the dead,
‪and I can handle the living.

538
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:33,199
‪This is my thing.
‪I'm on the Cold Case Unit.

539
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:34,867
‪How about we work together--

540
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:35,951
‪You're still here?

541
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:38,954
‪Yes.

542
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:42,291
‪Think about it. I'll wait for your call.

543
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:53,761
‪Let's go.

544
00:41:55,137 --> 00:41:55,971
‪Okay.

545
00:42:19,286 --> 00:42:20,788
‪"You're still here?"

546
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:26,877
‪I need a beer.

547
00:42:30,130 --> 00:42:31,257
<i>‪Ms. Cheon.</i>

548
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:32,883
‪Why don't we work together?

549
00:42:32,967 --> 00:42:35,761
‪You can handle the dead,
‪and I can handle the living.

550
00:42:39,723 --> 00:42:41,767
‪-Let's go, Ma.
‪-What?

551
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:10,170
‪Hey, Min-hwan.

552
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,299
‪It's me.

553
00:43:18,470 --> 00:43:21,807
‪Director Ok,
‪should we acquire another masterpiece?

554
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:24,602
‪Pardon?

555
00:43:24,685 --> 00:43:26,812
‪I like how our last purchase went.

556
00:43:26,895 --> 00:43:28,480
‪It was the easiest to clean up.

557
00:43:28,564 --> 00:43:30,399
‪Won't it be a bit too risky

558
00:43:31,108 --> 00:43:33,068
‪to employ the same tactic twice?

559
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:35,654
‪You see, the thing is…

560
00:43:35,738 --> 00:43:36,697
‪CEO KANG MIN-HWAN

561
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:38,532
‪Goodness, excuse me.

562
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:40,618
‪Hey, Mr. Kang.

563
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:42,578
‪Yes, what is it, Min-hwan?

564
00:43:44,204 --> 00:43:45,331
‪What?

565
00:43:46,290 --> 00:43:47,625
‪Cheon Yeo-ri did?

566
00:43:55,466 --> 00:43:56,550
‪Ms. Cheon.

567
00:43:57,176 --> 00:43:59,803
‪-Hello, I'm Cheon Yeo-ri.
‪-Goodness.

568
00:43:59,887 --> 00:44:01,972
‪I didn't get to introduce myself
‪properly yesterday.

569
00:44:02,056 --> 00:44:03,807
‪Oh, about that.

570
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:06,769
‪You must've been so disappointed.

571
00:44:06,852 --> 00:44:09,438
‪-It was such a humiliation.
‪-Not at all.

572
00:44:09,521 --> 00:44:12,232
‪I've hosted enough events to know
‪that things happen,

573
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:13,734
‪however well you're prepared.

574
00:44:15,444 --> 00:44:17,738
‪Thank you for being so understanding.

575
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:20,491
‪I wondered why

576
00:44:20,574 --> 00:44:24,328
‪you'd take so much interest
‪in something like this.

577
00:44:24,411 --> 00:44:28,082
‪Min-hwan tells me you studied
‪Archaeology and Art History.

578
00:44:29,124 --> 00:44:32,711
‪I assumed you'd have studied
‪Hotel Management or something like that.

579
00:44:32,795 --> 00:44:34,672
‪Thank you for your time, Director.

580
00:44:34,755 --> 00:44:36,131
‪Don't mention it.

581
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:38,258
‪You can ask me anything you want.

582
00:44:39,468 --> 00:44:41,970
‪May I ask who drew these portraits?

583
00:44:42,638 --> 00:44:43,722
‪Oh, yes.

584
00:44:44,807 --> 00:44:46,475
‪That would be Dowon.

585
00:44:46,558 --> 00:44:49,061
‪He wasn't acknowledged
‪or appreciated in his time.

586
00:44:51,480 --> 00:44:54,983
‪Could I take another look
‪at the love letter?

587
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:56,276
‪Yes, of course.

588
00:44:56,860 --> 00:44:57,986
‪Come this way.

589
00:45:01,365 --> 00:45:04,368
‪If this was found while relocating
‪Prince Gangpyeong's tomb,

590
00:45:04,451 --> 00:45:07,496
‪then was this love letter found
‪inside his coffin?

591
00:45:07,996 --> 00:45:08,997
‪Yes.

592
00:45:10,499 --> 00:45:12,793
‪Don't you find that so romantic?

593
00:45:12,876 --> 00:45:15,629
‪He must've yearned for her so deeply

594
00:45:15,712 --> 00:45:18,590
‪to have taken this letter
‪with him to death.

595
00:45:29,601 --> 00:45:32,563
<i>‪It would have been a scandal in their day.</i>

596
00:45:33,063 --> 00:45:36,233
<i>‪Prince Gangpyeong was a royal</i>
<i>‪who loved a woman beneath his class,</i>

597
00:45:36,316 --> 00:45:39,987
<i>‪a </i>‪gisaeng,<i>‪ a courtesan,</i>
<i>‪enough to make her his second wife.</i>

598
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:48,203
<i>‪Where was Hwagyeongdang buried then?</i>

599
00:45:48,287 --> 00:45:50,581
‪According to the story
‪told over generations,

600
00:45:50,664 --> 00:45:54,376
‪Prince Gangpyeong took her
‪on an excursion to Mt. Geumgang,

601
00:45:54,460 --> 00:45:57,296
<i>‪where Hwagyeongdang vanished</i>
<i>‪without</i>‪ a <i>‪trace.</i>

602
00:45:58,505 --> 00:46:02,050
‪One version of the story says
‪she became an immortal hermit.

603
00:46:03,886 --> 00:46:06,722
‪I suppose that's how legends are made.

604
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:15,189
‪Isn't it beautiful?

605
00:46:17,024 --> 00:46:21,528
‪Even down in the south,
‪such bright red camellias are rare.

606
00:46:22,196 --> 00:46:26,783
‪This isn't the time of year
‪for them to be in full bloom like that.

607
00:46:26,867 --> 00:46:29,745
‪So for the flowers to bloom
‪all of a sudden

608
00:46:29,828 --> 00:46:32,915
‪can only be a sign
‪of good things to come.

609
00:46:34,124 --> 00:46:36,126
‪What do you mean by that?

610
00:46:36,210 --> 00:46:40,506
‪The camellias must've known
‪that the love letter would be found.

611
00:46:41,089 --> 00:46:42,424
‪Just look at that sight.

612
00:46:51,934 --> 00:46:53,810
‪Here. Now get to it.

613
00:46:53,894 --> 00:46:56,396
‪-It's just a rumor, okay?
‪-Okay.

614
00:46:57,231 --> 00:46:59,191
‪A prosecutor went abroad
‪on a business trip

615
00:46:59,274 --> 00:47:01,193
‪and bought a pretty expensive painting.

616
00:47:01,276 --> 00:47:02,736
‪Since when do prosecutors do that?

617
00:47:02,819 --> 00:47:04,863
‪It's verified that they bought a painting,

618
00:47:04,947 --> 00:47:06,573
‪but there's no record of it
‪clearing customs.

619
00:47:07,991 --> 00:47:11,370
‪If customs has no record of it,
‪then either it didn't enter the country

620
00:47:11,453 --> 00:47:14,414
‪or someone powerful enough
‪to override customs was involved.

621
00:47:15,874 --> 00:47:17,584
‪A diplomatic pouch or Air Force One?

622
00:47:18,752 --> 00:47:21,755
‪That must've let off serious smoke.
‪Why didn't they dig further?

623
00:47:22,339 --> 00:47:23,590
‪It's not that they didn't. They couldn't.

624
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:26,385
‪The person who bought the painting

625
00:47:28,303 --> 00:47:29,763
‪was Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong.

626
00:47:30,722 --> 00:47:34,685
‪His older sister is Director Ok Gye-hui
‪of Reina Hotels & Resorts.

627
00:47:35,185 --> 00:47:36,478
‪Do you see where this is going?

628
00:47:38,063 --> 00:47:42,609
‪Does that mean Director Ok is involved
‪in Reina's money-laundering scheme?

629
00:47:43,402 --> 00:47:46,321
‪Whether it's money laundering or bribery,

630
00:47:46,405 --> 00:47:49,032
‪someone inside Reina
‪could be up to something.

631
00:47:52,035 --> 00:47:54,496
‪No way. I knew it.

632
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:55,539
‪Knew what?

633
00:47:55,622 --> 00:47:57,791
‪Look. They're birds of a feather.

634
00:47:57,874 --> 00:47:59,459
‪REINA'S CHEON YEO-RI
‪DATING CL SUCCESSOR KANG MIN-HWAN

635
00:47:59,543 --> 00:48:01,753
‪THE PAIR ATTENDED
‪AN OFFICIAL EVENT TOGETHER…

636
00:48:03,297 --> 00:48:04,131
‪What the…

637
00:48:05,048 --> 00:48:07,342
‪They were dating?

638
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:13,765
‪REINA'S CHEON YEO-RI
‪DATING CL SUCCESSOR KANG MIN-HWAN

639
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:20,814
‪You seem to have solved
‪another case by the river.

640
00:48:20,897 --> 00:48:22,691
‪That's what I do as usual.

641
00:48:24,526 --> 00:48:26,778
‪-Investigator Ko?
‪-Yes?

642
00:48:26,862 --> 00:48:28,697
‪Have we been getting any tip-offs?

643
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:33,327
‪You know, like we did for Mt. Haewang
‪or the river body case.

644
00:48:33,410 --> 00:48:35,871
‪No, we haven't gotten any recently.

645
00:48:35,954 --> 00:48:39,124
‪Well, have you been slacking lately?

646
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:41,543
‪Or maybe things have
‪fallen through the cracks.

647
00:48:41,627 --> 00:48:44,755
‪If you say that,
‪that would be my sign to burst into tears.

648
00:48:44,838 --> 00:48:46,548
‪I'd be so hurt and upset.

649
00:48:46,632 --> 00:48:51,970
‪I don't know what riled you up so badly
‪that you're taking it out on me…

650
00:48:52,054 --> 00:48:53,680
‪-I'm not riled up.
‪-Okay.

651
00:48:53,764 --> 00:48:57,559
‪We're supposed to solve cold cases,
‪but it's way too quiet.

652
00:48:57,643 --> 00:49:00,354
‪Did you leave your post for hours
‪when you were on night duty?

653
00:49:00,437 --> 00:49:02,356
‪-You too.
‪-What? No.

654
00:49:02,439 --> 00:49:03,690
‪-Come on, man.
‪-What?

655
00:49:03,774 --> 00:49:05,442
‪No, sorry. I mean, Mr. Ma.

656
00:49:05,525 --> 00:49:07,361
‪Right. Mr. Ma.

657
00:49:07,444 --> 00:49:09,821
‪If that's how you feel, from now on,

658
00:49:09,905 --> 00:49:12,991
‪whenever I get a work call
‪or need to use the bathroom,

659
00:49:13,075 --> 00:49:15,327
‪I'll call you to report
‪every single detail.

660
00:49:15,410 --> 00:49:17,037
‪So that you're satisfied.

661
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:18,622
‪That's it.

662
00:49:18,705 --> 00:49:22,376
‪That's why I must be involved,
‪even when it's you on night duty.

663
00:49:23,043 --> 00:49:25,671
‪Be sure to call me
‪especially if you get any tip-offs.

664
00:49:25,754 --> 00:49:26,838
‪Okay? You too, Hyeong-min.

665
00:49:26,922 --> 00:49:28,674
‪-Yes, of course.
‪-Okay.

666
00:49:29,716 --> 00:49:30,759
‪We'll work really hard.

667
00:49:36,848 --> 00:49:38,058
‪I can see you.

668
00:49:51,488 --> 00:49:53,865
‪Min-hwan said it wasn't him. Was it you?

669
00:49:53,949 --> 00:49:55,075
‪Take a seat.

670
00:49:58,912 --> 00:50:01,623
‪It's not a marriage announcement,
‪so what's the big deal?

671
00:50:01,707 --> 00:50:04,126
‪-It's up by how many percent?
‪-Thirteen percent, ma'am.

672
00:50:04,710 --> 00:50:05,877
‪My goodness.

673
00:50:05,961 --> 00:50:08,880
‪That's how the market reacted
‪to Reina and CL.

674
00:50:08,964 --> 00:50:11,049
‪You said you'd give me time.

675
00:50:11,133 --> 00:50:12,300
‪And I will.

676
00:50:12,384 --> 00:50:14,720
‪But I also need you
‪to give Min-hwan some hope.

677
00:50:16,304 --> 00:50:17,139
‪Grandma.

678
00:50:21,059 --> 00:50:23,478
‪-You can't barge in like that.
‪-I know what I'm doing.

679
00:50:30,944 --> 00:50:34,281
‪I heard the news about you and Min-hwan
‪was the chairwoman's idea.

680
00:50:34,364 --> 00:50:35,824
‪Did you ask her for a favor?

681
00:50:37,659 --> 00:50:40,537
‪I must ask, only out of pure curiosity.

682
00:50:41,663 --> 00:50:44,708
‪Are you doing this because
‪you really want to marry Min-hwan?

683
00:50:44,791 --> 00:50:45,709
‪Why do you care?

684
00:50:45,792 --> 00:50:47,043
‪This is insane.

685
00:50:47,836 --> 00:50:48,670
‪It's nonsensical.

686
00:50:48,754 --> 00:50:50,797
‪Why is it nonsensical?

687
00:50:50,881 --> 00:50:53,675
‪So you <i>‪are</i>‪ interested in marrying him.

688
00:50:54,718 --> 00:50:57,053
‪Min-hwan and Ji-hwan were brothers.

689
00:50:57,679 --> 00:51:00,223
‪If I were you, seeing Min-hwan
‪would remind me of Ji-hwan--

690
00:51:00,307 --> 00:51:01,141
‪Cheon Ha-ri.

691
00:51:04,019 --> 00:51:04,853
‪What?

692
00:51:04,936 --> 00:51:06,354
‪That's enough. Get out.

693
00:51:29,461 --> 00:51:30,921
‪NANGMAN SALTED BEEF TRIPE

694
00:51:31,004 --> 00:51:33,423
<i>‪No, you can't.</i>

695
00:51:33,507 --> 00:51:34,925
<i>‪Go away. Leave.</i>

696
00:51:39,471 --> 00:51:42,224
‪Nice, pork skin.
‪Weren't they good last time?

697
00:51:45,519 --> 00:51:47,646
‪That's one place,
‪and that's the other place.

698
00:51:47,729 --> 00:51:49,397
‪We're spoiled with options.

699
00:51:49,481 --> 00:51:51,066
‪You don't know
‪how addictive pork skin is.

700
00:51:51,149 --> 00:51:53,276
‪Gang-uk, are you going for dinner?

701
00:51:54,986 --> 00:51:56,571
‪-Hello.
‪-You're walking arm-in-arm?

702
00:51:56,655 --> 00:51:59,449
‪-Are you eating out?
‪-Ms. Im, do you like pork skin?

703
00:51:59,533 --> 00:52:02,160
‪-I love pork skin.
‪-Great, then we can…

704
00:52:02,244 --> 00:52:04,371
‪How about we go over there?
‪Their pork skin is amazing.

705
00:52:04,454 --> 00:52:06,832
‪-You should join us.
‪-Sounds good.

706
00:52:06,915 --> 00:52:09,042
‪You can go and enjoy yourselves.

707
00:52:09,125 --> 00:52:10,669
‪-We reserved a table…
‪-Come on in.

708
00:52:10,752 --> 00:52:12,587
‪-Let's all eat together.
‪-I have to go.

709
00:52:12,671 --> 00:52:14,047
‪Why leave when you came all this way?

710
00:52:14,130 --> 00:52:15,382
‪I need to work late today.

711
00:52:15,465 --> 00:52:17,259
‪You work late more often than you eat.

712
00:52:17,342 --> 00:52:20,929
‪-Eat with us before you go.
‪-I'll just buy something on the way back.

713
00:52:21,012 --> 00:52:23,598
‪Enjoy your meal
‪with Pil-dong and Hyeong-min.

714
00:52:25,517 --> 00:52:27,769
‪-You're actually leaving?
‪-Enjoy yourself!

715
00:52:30,939 --> 00:52:31,857
‪All right, attention!

716
00:52:32,816 --> 00:52:35,944
‪Everyone who's waited for their turn,
‪show yourselves now.

717
00:52:44,661 --> 00:52:47,789
‪Today, it's not first-come, first-served.
‪I'll pick based on your predicament.

718
00:52:48,748 --> 00:52:51,877
‪"The vile one who got me
‪deserves nothing but a beating."

719
00:52:51,960 --> 00:52:55,380
‪"I want to make sure
‪they pay the price and rot in prison."

720
00:52:55,463 --> 00:52:56,298
‪Who has that kind of story?

721
00:52:58,174 --> 00:52:59,509
‪Talk to me.

722
00:53:02,095 --> 00:53:03,555
‪You first.

723
00:53:04,639 --> 00:53:06,892
‪3 DAYS AGO

724
00:53:06,975 --> 00:53:08,894
‪It was somewhere here.

725
00:53:08,977 --> 00:53:10,937
‪Can we just call it a day and go home?

726
00:53:11,855 --> 00:53:15,400
‪It looks like it'll rain soon,
‪and I have a bad feeling.

727
00:53:15,483 --> 00:53:18,445
‪It's fine. I saw a really pretty one here.

728
00:53:19,029 --> 00:53:21,156
‪-It's somewhere here.
‪-You did?

729
00:53:22,240 --> 00:53:24,117
‪-You're sure it's nearby?
‪-This is it.

730
00:53:24,618 --> 00:53:25,619
‪-Look.
‪-Really?

731
00:53:26,703 --> 00:53:27,662
‪Wow.

732
00:53:28,747 --> 00:53:30,081
‪You really found it.

733
00:53:31,750 --> 00:53:33,335
‪It's beautiful.

734
00:53:33,418 --> 00:53:35,378
‪Come and have a look.

735
00:54:02,614 --> 00:54:03,615
‪Hello?

736
00:54:19,547 --> 00:54:21,758
‪I should've stamped your fingerprint
‪before letting you go.

737
00:54:24,636 --> 00:54:26,179
‪I forgot about that, honey.

738
00:54:32,769 --> 00:54:34,813
‪WRITTEN WILL

739
00:54:43,488 --> 00:54:44,364
‪Who's there?

740
00:54:44,447 --> 00:54:46,616
‪Talk about killing someone twice.

741
00:54:47,325 --> 00:54:49,494
‪How could one come back to do that?

742
00:54:54,082 --> 00:54:55,875
‪A bastard like him
‪doesn't deserve to be human.

743
00:55:02,465 --> 00:55:04,509
‪Are you on your own? This late at night?

744
00:55:04,592 --> 00:55:07,387
‪Would I have come here with a lover,
‪this late at night?

745
00:55:07,470 --> 00:55:09,514
‪If you're a passerby, just pass on by.

746
00:55:10,348 --> 00:55:11,683
‪Why see something you shouldn't?

747
00:55:12,559 --> 00:55:14,436
‪I wish I could unsee that too.

748
00:55:14,519 --> 00:55:16,980
‪Oh, is that so?

749
00:55:21,609 --> 00:55:22,777
‪Damn it.

750
00:55:30,035 --> 00:55:31,327
‪You're not a bad fighter.

751
00:55:50,263 --> 00:55:52,515
‪Who are you? Who the hell are you?

752
00:55:52,599 --> 00:55:54,559
‪-Let go.
‪-Damn it.

753
00:56:02,525 --> 00:56:05,862
‪I'll make you regret this.

754
00:56:07,238 --> 00:56:08,573
‪What should I go for?

755
00:56:09,991 --> 00:56:10,992
‪Your face?

756
00:56:14,829 --> 00:56:15,663
‪You punk!

757
00:56:26,341 --> 00:56:27,717
‪Get out of the way, Yeo-ri!

758
00:56:58,832 --> 00:57:00,208
‪-Mr. Ma.
‪-Wait.

759
00:57:00,291 --> 00:57:02,168
‪I'm fine. I'm fine, really.

760
00:57:03,044 --> 00:57:04,212
‪Are you two an item?

761
00:57:05,255 --> 00:57:06,381
‪You have a knife?

762
00:57:10,760 --> 00:57:12,011
‪Damn it.

763
00:57:19,519 --> 00:57:20,603
‪-That hurts.
‪-Keep still.

764
00:57:22,063 --> 00:57:24,274
‪-Damn you.
‪-Are you okay, Yeo-ri?

765
00:57:25,984 --> 00:57:26,901
‪Okay.

766
00:58:02,479 --> 00:58:04,731
‪Let go of me, damn it!

767
00:58:06,065 --> 00:58:08,234
‪I saw your face, you punk.

768
00:58:08,318 --> 00:58:09,694
‪Sure, whatever.

769
00:58:25,001 --> 00:58:28,004
‪Seeing ghosts
‪isn't some kind of superpower.

770
00:58:28,087 --> 00:58:31,925
‪How can you be so fearless,
‪coming alone to a mountain this late?

771
00:58:32,550 --> 00:58:35,553
‪That's why I called in a report
‪before coming here.

772
00:58:35,637 --> 00:58:37,722
‪I cover all my bases
‪before I set in motion.

773
00:58:37,805 --> 00:58:39,933
‪Right. Then what was that just now?

774
00:58:40,016 --> 00:58:42,560
‪You could've been badly hurt
‪if not for me.

775
00:58:45,021 --> 00:58:48,358
‪Aren't you the one
‪who could've been badly hurt?

776
00:58:48,942 --> 00:58:51,528
‪How could you not even
‪land a kick properly?

777
00:58:52,362 --> 00:58:53,821
‪That was a mistake.

778
00:58:53,905 --> 00:58:57,116
‪I trained in taekwondo,
‪judo, hapkido, and boxing.

779
00:58:57,200 --> 00:58:58,785
‪You don't know how fit I am.

780
00:58:58,868 --> 00:59:00,828
‪Oh, you're so fit and well-trained

781
00:59:00,912 --> 00:59:03,456
‪that you can't land a kick
‪when it actually counts?

782
00:59:03,540 --> 00:59:04,457
‪I thought

783
00:59:05,041 --> 00:59:08,086
‪you'd thrown out your back
‪because of the way you landed.

784
00:59:08,169 --> 00:59:10,547
‪You're so cruel.

785
00:59:10,630 --> 00:59:14,217
‪I was on standby for days on end,
‪working late in case you called.

786
00:59:14,300 --> 00:59:15,385
‪You're not the police.

787
00:59:15,468 --> 00:59:18,263
‪What prosecutor works late
‪to wait for a tip-off?

788
00:59:18,346 --> 00:59:19,639
‪Are all prosecutors like that?

789
00:59:19,722 --> 00:59:22,058
‪No other prosecutor does this.

790
00:59:22,141 --> 00:59:23,810
‪I do it only because of you…

791
00:59:26,604 --> 00:59:27,438
‪What I mean is…

792
00:59:28,565 --> 00:59:34,028
‪I mean, I'm in charge of cold cases,
‪and we both used to see ghosts.

793
00:59:34,112 --> 00:59:35,697
‪I can't just turn a blind eye.

794
00:59:36,364 --> 00:59:37,865
‪Only my life is back to normal,

795
00:59:37,949 --> 00:59:41,661
‪while you stay up at night
‪because of ghosts.

796
00:59:43,079 --> 00:59:43,913
‪Right?

797
00:59:50,211 --> 00:59:52,171
‪So from what I gather,

798
00:59:53,214 --> 00:59:55,300
‪it looks like you're getting engaged
‪to your boyfriend.

799
00:59:56,217 --> 00:59:58,886
‪It said we were dating,
‪not that we were engaged.

800
01:00:00,096 --> 01:00:02,599
‪So it's true that you're dating him?

801
01:00:03,099 --> 01:00:04,976
‪That false report will be corrected soon.

802
01:00:05,059 --> 01:00:06,561
‪What? "False report"?

803
01:00:07,937 --> 01:00:09,230
‪It's a false report?

804
01:00:11,107 --> 01:00:11,983
‪Yes, and besides…

805
01:00:13,610 --> 01:00:15,445
‪Why do you care if I'm dating or not?

806
01:00:16,362 --> 01:00:22,201
‪You showed up to a special event
‪with your girlfriend proudly on your arm.

807
01:00:22,285 --> 01:00:23,119
‪"Special event"?

808
01:00:25,038 --> 01:00:26,289
‪You mean the art gallery?

809
01:00:26,372 --> 01:00:29,459
‪I didn't link arms with her.
‪She clung to me like that.

810
01:00:29,542 --> 01:00:31,210
‪She is not my girlfriend.

811
01:00:31,294 --> 01:00:33,755
‪She and I are like…

812
01:00:33,838 --> 01:00:36,007
‪We could never get close.

813
01:00:37,467 --> 01:00:40,053
‪We're like the Earth and the moon.

814
01:00:40,136 --> 01:00:41,971
‪That's how far apart we are.

815
01:00:43,139 --> 01:00:45,975
‪-Like the Earth and the moon?
‪-Yes.

816
01:00:46,059 --> 01:00:49,395
‪How lovely.
‪Those two always come as a pair.

817
01:00:50,897 --> 01:00:55,568
‪Are you upset
‪that Im and I showed up as a pair?

818
01:00:55,652 --> 01:00:57,403
‪I'm just stating a fact.

819
01:00:58,154 --> 01:01:00,114
‪Did I say I was upset?

820
01:01:03,660 --> 01:01:06,954
‪Well then, instead of
‪the Earth and the moon,

821
01:01:07,038 --> 01:01:10,208
‪how about we call it Neptune?

822
01:01:10,291 --> 01:01:12,085
‪Would you feel any less upset?

823
01:01:12,168 --> 01:01:14,045
‪I never said I was upset.

824
01:01:14,128 --> 01:01:15,254
‪Not that then.

825
01:01:15,338 --> 01:01:17,715
‪Then how about Andromeda?

826
01:01:17,799 --> 01:01:19,384
‪Andromeda sounds much better.

827
01:01:20,551 --> 01:01:21,386
‪Doesn't it?

828
01:01:21,969 --> 01:01:23,805
‪Is there anything farther away than that?

829
01:01:24,389 --> 01:01:25,431
‪A black hole?

830
01:01:27,225 --> 01:01:29,227
‪Not even a goodbye? Can't you at least…

831
01:01:30,395 --> 01:01:32,230
‪Can't she at least say goodbye?

832
01:01:33,231 --> 01:01:34,273
‪She didn't even bother.

833
01:02:21,195 --> 01:02:23,614
‪You said you handled cold cases.

834
01:02:24,115 --> 01:02:24,949
‪Yes.

835
01:02:26,033 --> 01:02:26,993
‪Shall we take it on?

836
01:02:28,661 --> 01:02:30,621
‪A 300-year-old cold case.

837
01:02:31,748 --> 01:02:32,665
‪Let's work together.

838
01:03:03,571 --> 01:03:05,490
‪FIND ME

839
01:03:23,925 --> 01:03:26,344
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

840
01:03:26,427 --> 01:03:29,722
<i>‪It's not the Joseon-era version of </i>‪Ghost,
<i>‪but a total psychopath.</i>

841
01:03:29,806 --> 01:03:32,225
<i>‪We'll do whatever it takes to find a way.</i>

842
01:03:32,308 --> 01:03:34,101
<i>‪There's no such thing as a perfect crime.</i>

843
01:03:34,185 --> 01:03:36,437
‪What must be revealed will come to light.

844
01:03:36,521 --> 01:03:39,315
‪I need you to check that.
‪That's the part that involves the living.

845
01:03:39,398 --> 01:03:42,693
‪This looks more like
‪Ms. Cheon's part than mine.

846
01:03:42,777 --> 01:03:46,197
‪Do you think Yeo-ri is actually onto us?

847
01:03:46,280 --> 01:03:47,990
‪Yes, hello, Ms. Cheon.

848
01:03:48,491 --> 01:03:51,202
<i>‪Are these all the artworks</i>
<i>‪displayed around the hotel?</i>

849
01:03:51,285 --> 01:03:52,912
‪Why do you want to know that so badly?

850
01:03:54,205 --> 01:03:55,540
‪What is this?

851
01:03:55,623 --> 01:03:58,167
‪I got them on my business trip to Europe.
‪I thought they'd suit you.

852
01:03:58,251 --> 01:04:00,711
<i>‪I read the article about you two.</i>
<i>‪Congratulations.</i>

853
01:04:00,795 --> 01:04:03,172
‪Are Cheon Yeo-ri and Min-hwan
‪actually dating?

854
01:04:03,256 --> 01:04:06,759
<i>‪Min-hwan will be able to support you</i>
<i>‪more than enough.</i>

855
01:04:06,843 --> 01:04:09,470
<i>‪Why are you so hard to reach?</i>
<i>‪You said you'd call me back.</i>

856
01:04:09,554 --> 01:04:12,765
<i>‪I might have to get engaged.</i>

857
01:04:13,349 --> 01:04:14,392
‪What?

858
01:04:14,475 --> 01:04:19,188
‪Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
